The button is connected between D4 and GND. When the button is pressed, the counter never goes up. What causes the bug in the program?

```
volatile unsigned int basis = 0;

void say() {
  basis++;
}

void setup() {
  Serial.begin(9600);
  pinMode(4, INPUT_PULLUP);
  attachInterrupt(digitalPinToInterrupt(4), say, FALLING);
}

void loop() {
  Serial.println(basis);
  delay(500);
}
```

An ideal button (no bounce) is pressed and released only once; this finishes within the first 2 seconds. What is the first value printed?

```
volatile int sayac = 0;

void kes() {
  sayac++;
}

void setup() {
  Serial.begin(9600);
  pinMode(2, INPUT_PULLUP);
  attachInterrupt(digitalPinToInterrupt(2), kes, CHANGE);
}

void loop() {
  delay(2000);
  Serial.println(sayac);
}
```
